A||||10||3fifty||Temp Guage||||5||
Z||000000||3fifty||01-15-2001||10:19 PM||||Temp guage pegs when ignition is switched on, and then drops back. Does not read as car runs. Does that sound like a guage<BR>,sending unit, or what? Thanks for any help.<P>85 GT V6  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||01-15-2001||10:45 PM||||It is normal for the temp gauge to peg when starting the car.  <P>It sounds like the sending unit might be bad.  You should be able to check it with an ohm meter.  Compare the reading when cold and when at normal operating temp.  The sending unit is easy to get to at the rear of the block near the distributor.  It will have 2 pins, 1 for the gauge needle and one for the warning light.  You can tell which is which with the ohm meter.  The warning light will test as an open circuit while the gauge needle will have a resistance value that gets lower (i think) as it warms up.  Just test each pin to ground and see what the reading is.<P>You can also test the warning light and needle by shorting each wire to ground with the ignition on and see the light and needle react.  If the needle swings when grounded, it is most likely the sending unit.  Cheap and easy to replace.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||01-16-2001||02:08 AM||||If you want to end the "pegging" temp gauge check out link below.<P> <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierogt88||01-16-2001||09:19 AM||||Mine is pegged too...<BR>but it doesn't come back down...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/0115_019.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||01-16-2001||10:06 AM||||FieroGT88, The reason yours is stuck is because it possibly pegged and stuck in the foam rubber seal. Since you need to remove the face to perform the fix you can then loosen the needle and trim the foam back a bit.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||01-17-2001||12:43 AM||||Mine would get stuck on hot summer days.. a few good smacks on the top of the panel and it would pop back down  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||
Z||000006||FIEROCIOUS||01-17-2001||03:37 AM||||Check out fiero online service guide it gives you diagrams to re-wire the gauge. It was a factory boo boo that all Fieros have.<BR>Mine used to peg but I switched the wires since and it works perfect! It was easy to do too!||||reg||1
