Z||000008||Bob Englert||01-17-2001||09:22 PM||||mblackwell:<P>Sounds like your sending unit might have failed.  It is very easy to replace.  I would defenitely want to have the temp gauge working on my Fiero!<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000009||mblackwell||01-17-2001||09:59 PM||||Where is the sending unit and where do I get a new one?  I don't know much about cars.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000010||tgowens||01-18-2001||01:23 AM||||the sending unit is in approximately the 8 o'clock position from the #5 spark plug on the left side of the rear of the engine next to the manifold. Usually (due to the high heat from the manifold) the plug will get brittle and break but you will see the sensor there - it has a strange somewhat half round keyed plug end where the wire connector fits.........best description I can give you of its location.........||||reg||1
